  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Title written in pencil on half title of book block of: Silence : lectures and writings / John Cage.  1st ed.  Middleton, Conn. : Wesleyan University Press, c. 1961.  276 p.  Without covers, the block has been fused top and bottom, each page trimmed by increasingly deep tearing to form a textured, rising block displaying letters from the text of each page providing both visual and tactile sensations as well as expressing the artist's concept of the book.  The half title of the original is full size at the base.  All after p. 230 reduced to inner margin only.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">No. 39 of 46 in "Pages" series created by Spector in the period 1982-1987.--This and other information from the artist.  In an interview, Spector distinguishes these works from "artists' books" as being interpretive transformations.</subfield>
  </datafield>
